38:## A11.2 P3's verification profile: floor and duty
39-
40-**The proofs are unchanged.** P3's model half assumes a verifier with stated behaviour. The assumption half is
41-bounded implementation evidence that the shipped verifier has that behaviour. It does not show that every model
42-assumption is preserved in general.
43-
44-1. **Fields kept.** All six of A1's fields stay. For each algorithm in the governing specification they are read as
45-   follows:
46-
47-   | A1 field | ECDSA P-256 (rule O) | ML-DSA-65 (rule R) |
48-   |---|---|---|
49-   | exact library and version | `cryptography` and its bundled OpenSSL, identified by wheel tag and native-library SHA-256 | same |
50-   | accepted signature encodings | OpenPGP v4 packet; MPI rules; r, s ∈ [1, n−1]; rule-O policy | exact 3309 bytes; strict hint and z encoding |
51-   | public-key validation | exact uncompressed point; coordinates < p; on the curve; checked before the library | exact SPKI; no algebraic validation exists |
52-   | low-order-point handling | cofactor 1: infinity rejected as a key and as the equation's result; invalid-curve points rejected | no referent. Replaced by: degenerate-key behaviour recorded |
53-   | cofactor equation variant | cofactor 1: a single variant; x(R) reduced mod n | no referent. Replaced by: the FIPS 204 interface (pure, empty context), with every other interface rejected |
54-   | negative vectors for each | owner vectors plus Wycheproof | owner vectors plus Wycheproof |
